            I am new to BlueZ programming and like to know the return value
of sdp_uuid128_create(). According "sdp_lib.h" this function returns a value
of type 'uuid_t'. This function takes two parameters and converts four 32
bit integers to a valid UUID (first parameter). But what does that return
value indicate? How can I check whether sdp_uuid128_create() is successfully
executed or not ? I couldn't find any documentation for all these sdp_lib
apis. Can anybody give me any useful link?    
            
Regards,
